{"reference":"Judges 20","book":"Judges","chapter":20,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Larger Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Read alongside Judges 19 and 21, the civil war in this chapter forms part of a closing sequence marked by sexual violence, escalating warfare, collective punishment, and forced wife-taking. This portrayal is understood as evidence of social collapse, not as a moral pattern for imitation.","verse_refs":["Judges 19","Judges 21:1-25"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_020_60be7403803f23de582c207e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}